ned, but the\n        oldest frames of a traceback are returned.  (This matches the\n        behavior of the traceback module.)\n\n        For reasons beyond our control, only one stack frame is\n        returned for a suspended coroutine.\n        ")), Return(value=Call(func=Attribute(value=Name(id='base_tasks'), attr='_task_get_stack'), args=[Name(id='self'), Name(id='limit')]))]), FunctionDef(name='print_stack', args=arguments(args=[arg(arg='self')], kwonlyargs=[arg(arg='limit'), arg(arg='file')], kw_defaults=[Constant(value=None), Constant(value=None)]), body=[Expr(value=Constant(value="Print the stack or traceback for this task's coroutine.\n\n        This produces output similar to that of the traceback module,\n        for the frames retrieved by get_stack().  The limit argument\n        is passed to get_stack().  The file argument is an I/O stream\n        to which the output is written; by default output is written\n        to sys.stderr.\n        ")), Return(value=Call(func=Attribute(value=Name(id='base_tasks'), attr='_task_print_stack'), args=[Name(id='self'), Name(id='limit'), Name(id='file')]))]), FunctionDef(name='cancel', args=arguments(args=[arg(arg='self'), arg(arg='msg')], defaults=[Constant(value=None)]), body=[Expr(value=Constant(value="Request that this task cancel itself.\n\n        This arranges for a CancelledError to be thrown into the\n        wrapped coroutine on the next cycle through the event loop.\n        The coroutine then has a chance to clean up or even deny\n        the request using try/except/finally.\n\n        Unlike Future.cancel, this does not guarantee that the\n        task will be cancelled: the exception might be caught and\n        acted upon, delaying cancellation of the task or preventing\n        cancellation completely.  The task may also return a value or\n        raise a different exception.\n\n        Immediately after this method is called, Task.cancelled() will\n        not return True (unless the task was already cancelled).  A\n        task will be marked as cancelled when the wrapped coroutine\n        terminates with a CancelledError exception (even if cancel()\n        was not called).\n\n        This also increases the task's count of cancellation requests.\n        ")), Assign(targets=[Attribute(value=Name(id='self'), attr='_log_traceback', ctx=Store())], value=Constant(value=False)), If(test=Call(func=Attribute(value=Name(id='self'), attr='done')), body=[Return(value=Constant(value=False))]), AugAssign(target=Attribute(value=Name(id='self'), attr='_num_cancels_requested', ctx=Store()), op=Add(), value=Constant(value=1)), If(test=Compare(left=Attribute(value=Name(id='self'), attr='_fut_waiter'), ops=[IsNot()], comparators=[Constant(value=None)]), body=[If(test=Call(func=Attribute(value=Attribute(value=Name(id='self'), attr='_fut_waiter'), attr='cancel'), keywords=[keyword(arg='msg', value=Name(id='msg'))]), body=[Return(value=Constant(value=True))])]), Assign(targets=[Attribute(value=Name(id='self'), attr='_must_cancel', ctx=Store())], value=Constant(value=True)), Assign(targets=[Attribute(value=Name(id='self'), attr='_cancel_message', ctx=Store())], value=Name(id='msg')), Return(value=Constant(value=True))]), FunctionDef(name='cancelling', args=arguments(args=[arg(arg='self')]), body=[Expr(value=Constant(value="Return the count of the task's cancellation requests.\n\n        This count is incremented when .cancel() is called\n        and may be decremented using .uncancel().\n        ")), Return(value=Attribute(value=Name(id='self'), attr='_num_cancels_requested'))]), FunctionDef(name='uncancel', args=arguments(args=[arg(arg='self')]), body=[Expr(value=Constant(value="Decrement the task's count of cancellation requests.\n\n        This should be called by the party that called `cancel()` on the task\n        beforehand.\n\n        Returns the remaining number of cancellation requests.\n        ")), If(test=Compare(left=Attribute(value=Name(id='self'), attr='_num_c