immediately propagated to the returned\n    future.\n\n    Cancellation: if the outer Future is cancelled, all children (that\n    have not completed yet) are also cancelled.  If any child is\n    cancelled, this is treated as if it raised CancelledError --\n    the outer Future is *not* cancelled in this case.  (This is to\n    prevent the cancellation of one child to cause other children to\n    be cancelled.)\n\n    If *return_exceptions* is False, cancelling gather() after it\n    has been marked done won't cancel any submitted awaitables.\n    For instance, gather can be marked done after propagating an\n    exception to the caller, therefore, calling ``gather.cancel()``\n    after catching an exception (raised by one of the awaitables) from\n    gather won't cancel any other awaitables.\n    ")), If(test=UnaryOp(op=Not(), operand=Name(id='coros_or_futures')), body=[Assign(targets=[Name(id='loop', ctx=Store())], value=Call(func=Attribute(value=Name(id='events'), attr='get_event_loop'))), Assign(targets=[Name(id='outer', ctx=Store())], value=Call(func=Attribute(value=Name(id='loop'), attr='create_future'))), Expr(value=Call(func=Attribute(value=Name(id='outer'), attr='set_result'), args=[List()])), Return(value=Name(id='outer'))]), Assign(targets=[Name(id='loop', ctx=Store())], value=Call(func=Attribute(value=Name(id='events'), attr='_get_running_loop'))), If(test=Compare(left=Name(id='loop'), ops=[IsNot()], comparators=[Constant(value=None)]), body=[Assign(targets=[Name(id='cur_task', ctx=Store())], value=Call(func=Name(id='current_task'), args=[Name(id='loop')]))], orelse=[Assign(targets=[Name(id='cur_task', ctx=Store())], value=Constant(value=None))]), FunctionDef(name='_done_callback', args=arguments(args=[arg(arg='fut'), arg(arg='cur_task')], defaults=[Name(id='cur_task')]), body=[Nonlocal(names=['nfinished']), AugAssign(target=Name(id='nfinished', ctx=Store()), op=Add(), value=Constant(value=1)), If(test=Compare(left=Name(id='cur_task'), ops=[IsNot()], com